## 🏗️ Architecture: Universal MCP Design

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│         Agent Memory MCP                    │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                             │
│  Configuration:                             │
│  ├── ZERODB_API_URL (configurable!)        │
│  ├── ZERODB_USERNAME                        │
│  ├── ZERODB_PASSWORD                        │
│  └── ZERODB_PROJECT_ID                      │
│                                             │
│  Works with:                                │
│  ├── ✅ ZeroLocal (localhost:8000)         │
│  ├── ✅ ZeroDB Cloud (api.ainative.studio) │
│  ├── ✅ Self-hosted deployments            │
│  └── ✅ Any compatible endpoint            │
│                                             │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

---

## 🔧 ZeroLocal-Specific Features

### **Auto-Detection** (Coming Soon)

```javascript
// Automatically detect if ZeroLocal is running
const isLocal = await detectZeroLocal()

if (isLocal) {
  apiUrl = 'http://localhost:8000'
  console.log('✅ Using ZeroLocal')
} else {
  apiUrl = 'https://api.ainative.studio'
  console.log('☁️ Using ZeroDB Cloud')
}
```

### **Health Check Integration**

```javascript
// Check if ZeroLocal is healthy before connecting
const health = await fetch('http://localhost:8000/health')
const data = await health.json()

if (data.status === 'healthy') {
  console.log('✅ ZeroLocal is ready')
  console.log(`Services: ${Object.keys(data.services).length}`)
}
```

### **Local-First Fallback**

```javascript
// Try local first, fall back to cloud
try {
  return await api.call('http://localhost:8000/v1/...')
} catch (error) {
  console.log('⚠️ ZeroLocal not available, using cloud')
  return await api.call('https://api.ainative.studio/v1/...')
}
```

